meta {
  name: 04 Lab Orders List
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/patient-portal/lab-orders?page=1&limit=10
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  page: 1
  limit: 10
  ~patientId:
  ~search:
  ~dateFrom:
  ~dateTo:
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{patientAccessToken}}
}

script:post-response {
  const rows = res.getBody() && res.getBody().data;
  if (Array.isArray(rows) && rows[0]) bru.setEnvVar("patientLabOrderId", rows[0].orderId);
}

docs {
  The patient's lab orders (orders that carry a lab/diagnostics section), newest
  first, across every branch of the session's lab. Read-only.

  Scope comes from the patient JWT (tenant + person): the person's own record plus
  linked family members. Drafts, quotes and appointments never appear; cancelled
  orders do.

  Query (all optional):
  - `page` (default 1), `limit` (default 10, max 100)
  - `patientId` — narrow to ONE viewable patient (the "Viewing" dropdown). It is only
    ever intersected with the viewable patients: an id outside the scope returns an
    empty list, never someone else's orders.
  - `search` — order number, external order id, or a test/panel name
  - `dateFrom` / `dateTo` — inclusive ISO dates on the order date

  Response `data[]`:
  `{ orderId, orderNo, orderDate, patientId, patientName, branchName, branchCity,
     tests[], status, reportStatus, publishedReportCount, canDownloadReports, billStatus }`
  plus `meta: { total, page, limit, totalPages }`.

  - `orderNo` = external order id, else the order code.
  - `status` (testing progress, NOT publish state): `PENDING` (no test has reached
    reporting) | `IN_PROGRESS` | `PARTIALLY_COMPLETE` | `COMPLETE` (every test line is
    approved or published; a line with no report yet counts as unfinished) | `CANCELLED`.
  - `reportStatus`: `NOT_PUBLISHED` | `PARTIALLY_PUBLISHED` | `PUBLISHED`.
  - `canDownloadReports` is true only with at least one PUBLISHED report on a
    non-cancelled order.

  Requires a patient JWT (`403 PATIENT_PASSWORD_CHANGE_REQUIRED` on a temp-password
  session). A staff token gets `401`.
}
